# AI Stock Checker — Agent Rule

## Goal
Best local Docker stock/crypto checker + paper trader for a small friend group: low churn, honest docs, validated strategies.

## Must follow
- Secrets only via `.env` (see `.env.example`). Never hardcode API keys.
- Primary service: `intelligent-trader` in `docker-compose.yml`.
- Anti-churn defaults: min hold ≥4h, scan ≥15m, trade ≥5m.
- Filter stables/leveraged/noise via `stock_checker/symbol_filters.py`.
- Prefer Chrome MCP for live `pro.openbb.co` research (see `OPENBB.md`); do not invent OpenBB data.
- AI: instruct models only (`gemma4:latest`, `qwen3.5:9b`) — not coder models.
- No unverified performance claims in docs.
- Prefer Docker for deps; do not install on host.
- Keep `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` aligned with code.
- Continue unfinished work from `IMPROVEMENT.md` without waiting for a new user prompt when in an improvement loop.

## Git (commit + push ASAP)
- Follow `GIT.md`: commit after each verified change; push immediately when `origin` exists.
- Do **not** wait for the user to say “commit” or “push”.
- Never commit secrets/`data/`; never force-push `main`.

## Verify
`docker build -t ai-stock-checker . && docker run --rm ai-stock-checker pytest -q`
